 ## Governance, learning & enterprise layers
 
 Beyond the swarm kernel, `maverick-core` carries the subsystems that make
-Lightwork a *governed, self-improving* platform rather than a bare runtime. All
-are opt-in and additive (kernel rule 1 — the kernel runs unchanged with them
-off). See `docs/FEATURES.md` for depth.
+Lightwork a governed platform with several learning authority levels. They do
+not share one opt-in switch. Secure defaults enable audit signing, at-rest
+encryption and fail-closed high/critical-risk consent; deployment-specific
+identity, capability and egress settings have their own controls, with mandatory
+enterprise floors. Local and governed prompt/policy learning default on, while
+executable-tool generation, third-party MCP acquisition and extra learning
+provider egress require separate authority. Code self-modification remains an
+opt-in research path that proposes, evaluates and archives; it never applies or
+promotes live code. See `config.py`, `security_defaults.py`, `self_modify.py` and
+[runtime architecture](docs/architecture.md) for these boundaries.
 
