 ## Distribution channels
 
-`.github/workflows/release.yml` triggers on `git tag v*`:
-
-- **PyPI**: `maverick-agent` (squatted, so we ship under this name; the Python import name + CLI name remain `maverick`), `maverick-shield`, `maverick-dashboard`, `maverick-mcp-server`, `maverick-channels`, `maverick-installer`. Gated on `PYPI_API_TOKEN`.
-- **GHCR**: multi-tag Docker image — `:latest`, `:vX.Y.Z`, `:vX.Y`.
-- **GitHub Releases**: PyInstaller single-file binaries for Linux x86_64, macOS arm64, Windows x86_64, each **Sigstore-signed keyless** (cosign via GitHub OIDC — `.sig` + `.pem` per artifact, logged to Rekor; verify with `deploy/verify-release.sh`), plus a per-release CycloneDX SBOM.
+These are configured publication paths, not evidence that artifacts have shipped:
+
+- **Release cohort:** [release-cohort.toml](release-cohort.toml) defines the current
+  version and all eight Python distributions. The import and CLI remain `maverick`.
+- **PyPI:** [publish.yml](.github/workflows/publish.yml) publishes only the explicit
+  public allowlist after a successful Release workflow, using externally configured
+  OIDC trusted publishing. Manual dispatch is build-only.
+- **GHCR and GitHub Releases:** [release.yml](.github/workflows/release.yml) defines
+  tagged-main provenance checks, images, platform binaries, source archives,
+  checksums, SBOMs and Sigstore verification. Check the exact workflow run and
+  [release assets](https://github.com/Daybreak-AI-Labs/Lightwork/releases) before
+  relying on an artifact. Native Windows customer signing/acceptance is separate.
 
